## Why This Is Asked
Assess ability to design a practical NLP pipeline for enterprise chat, focusing on bilingual classification and fast retrieval within a Slack-like setting, plus drift detection and rollback strategies.

## Key Concepts
- Language detection
- TF-IDF features
- Logistic regression for intents
- Cosine similarity retrieval
- Bilingual KB management
- Drift monitoring and rollback

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: fit a per-language classifier and a bilingual retriever
const modelEN = trainLR(tfIdf(examplesEN), labelsEN);
const modelES = trainLR(tfIdf(examplesES), labelsES);

function predict(msg){
  const lang = detect(msg);
  const vec = tfIdf(msg, lang);
  const model = lang === 'en' ? modelEN : modelES;
  return model.predict(vec);
}
function retrieve(query){
  return kbArticles.findTopSimilar(query);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle slang and emojis?
- How would you test drift and plan rollbacks?

## Why This Is Asked
This evaluates practical design skills for privacy-preserving NLP systems, edge computing constraints, and multilingual text processing in real-world chat applications.

## Key Concepts
- Hybrid PII detection using regex rules and ML classification
- On-device inference with strict latency requirements (<150ms)
- Multilingual support and code-switching handling
- Configurable redaction policies and comprehensive audit logging
- Evaluation methodology combining offline metrics and staged rollout
- Automated rollback strategies for production safety

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode for multilingual PII redaction
function redactPII(text, language = 'auto') {
  const tokens = tokenizeMultilingual(text);
  const regexMatches = applyRegexRules(tokens);
  const mlPredictions = classifyContext(tokens, language);
  return mergeAndRedact(text, regexMatches, mlPredictions);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you balance false positives versus coverage in PII redaction?
- How would you monitor and maintain model performance across languages?
- What fallback mechanisms would you implement for edge cases?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests end-to-end design for high-stakes, multilingual NLP with strict latency, privacy, and governance constraints. Probes integration of retrieval-augmented detection, on-device preprocessing, drift-aware evaluation, explainability, and safe rollout strategies.

## Key Concepts

- Real-time streaming NLP
- Retrieval-augmented detection
- On-device PII redaction
- Multilingual DistilBERT variants
- Drift detection and governance
- Explainability and audit logging

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode for pipeline steps
async function infer(text, lang) {
  const redacted = redactPII(text, lang)
  const ctx = encode(redacted, lang)
  const evidence = retriever.search(redacted, lang)
  const score = detector.score(ctx, evidence)
  return { score, evidence }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you measure and bound the false positive rate across languages?
- How would you implement the rollback and audit logging in production?

